    <bpmn:userTask id="azeri-community" name="Writes posts and comments on /azeri">
      <bpmn:documentation>Anybody reads it; an account writes in it. A post — a title and a text in any language — or a comment, which may answer another; one's own changed or deleted; an upvote on anybody else's. Five posts and fifty comments a day. A dot on the tab, and a number before the browser's title, while another tab is read and there is something new. The site's owner may take anybody's down.
when: azeri_write
when: azeri_reply
ref: azeri.html
ref: assets/azeri.js</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>member-e1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>member-e2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="azeri-community-keep" name="Keeps what is written, the author's to change">
      <bpmn:documentation>Every write reads the row's owner first. A deleted post with comments under it, and every deleted comment, is emptied and kept so the conversation still reads; a score and a post's count of comments are counted again by the write that changes them.
ref: functions/api/azeri/community.js POST
ref: functions/api/_community.js</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>member-e2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>member-e3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="azeri-community-said" name="Posts, comments or upvotes">
      <bpmn:documentation>when: azeri_posted
when: azeri_comment
when: azeri_upvote</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>member-e3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
