    <bpmn:userTask id="walk" name="Walks a list">
      <bpmn:documentation>Any list they can read, on foot, by bike or both: starts a walk, checks in at each place with the phone's location, in any order and over as many days as it takes, can have the places left put in the shortest order from where they are standing, and may leave a comment where they checked in and one on the whole of it at the end, and say how they went round: on foot, by bike, by car or mixed. The board under the places opens: pressing anybody's time there shows how that person walked it, place by place in the order they really checked them, with the real gap between each pair.
when: walk_start
when: walk_check
when: walk_note
when: walk_reorder
when: walk_replan
when: walk_mode
when: walk_again
when: walk_map_open
when: walk_directions
when: walk_trace
ref: assets/walk.js
ref: assets/lists.js walkView()
ref: assets/app.js walkOnMap()</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>member-e21</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>member-e22</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="walk-check" name="Checks the nearest place within 75 m, keeps the place and the time">
      <bpmn:documentation>The location a check sends is compared and not kept.
when: walk_finish
ref: functions/api/walk.js POST start, mode, check, note, order, again</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>member-e22</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>member-e23</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="walk-done" name="Finished, on the list's board">
      <bpmn:incoming>member-e23</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="ride" name="Reads the bike rides they recorded">
      <bpmn:documentation>The Your rides card on the account page, there once they have a ride: all of them added up — how far, how long, the average and top speed, the fastest kilometre — over what each was called, how far, how long and the day. Nothing on the website records one — a ride is recorded in Rattatee, the iPhone app, and saved under the account it is signed in to.
ref: assets/account.js ridesCard()
ref: assets/account.js ridesTotals()
ref: functions/api/rides.js GET ?mine=1
ref: functions/api/_ridestats.js</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>member-e24</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>member-e25</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="ride-done" name="Their rides, listed">
